    "explanation": "This is the ruling on TRP-05017 of 9 September 2026. The case cannot be decided on the merits, so it goes to a human reviewer; no money moves now. Here is the reasoning, for both of you. (1) The deviation. On the platform's recorded distances, which POL-RD-22 requires be used, the trip ran 13.2 km against a recommended 12.0 km, a deviation of 1.20 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance. The GPS trace is not used to re-measure distance (it records 11.12 km, and POL-RD-22 says a sparse trace understates a route's length); it shows only which route was taken and when. Both sides' arithmetic here is accepted, and the duration figures (24.0 min against 21.8 min optimal, 8 min 44 s off the recommended route) do not change the distance measure. So the within-tolerance rows POL-RD-24(c) and (e) do not apply. (2) The traffic. The reroute was traffic-justified under POL-RD-23. The LTA advisory LTA-TI-260909-3941 records an ACCIDENT on the Central Expressway (CTE) towards SLE after the Braddell Road exit, valid 20:23:22 to 21:40:02, which covers both the trip window (20:40:02-21:04:02) and the point at which the vehicle left the recommended route (20:54:05); ACCIDENT is an admissible incident type; the CTE is the road the recommended route uses (optimal_route_via lists 'Central Expressway (CTE)'); and the Braddell Road exit named in the advisory is exactly where the vehicle left that route, so the advisory sits on the recommended route segment the driver avoided. The rider's argument that the advisory is not shown to intersect the route is rejected - the derived fields were left null precisely because the intersection was for the Judge to determine from road, direction and location, and they determine it. Row (d) of POL-RD-24 (not traffic-justified) therefore does not apply. (3) What cannot be established. Rows (a) and (b) of POL-RD-24 both turn on whether the driver informed the rider of the deviation before or at the point of deviation. POL-RD-21 permits a verbal notice only with the trip call recording as evidence, and states in terms that a verbal notice with no recording in the record cannot be established. There is no recording: the trip record's in_app_calls list is empty and the evidence contains no audio. The chat log is complete but its only two messages (20:38:52 and 20:39:12) pre-date the trip and concern the pickup point, so they are neither a notice of the deviation nor the rider's acknowledgment of one. We therefore cannot establish that the driver notified the rider, and we cannot establish that he did not; the rider's statement is a denial, and no rule lets us decide the notification point either way. Row (a) (no refund) needs the rider informed and agreeing; row (b) (refund of the excess distance fare) needs the rider not informed. Neither can be applied. (4) The outcome. POL-RD-24 requires that exactly one row apply and sends a case that fits no row to escalation, and POL-GEN-26 requires escalation where a fact a rule needs cannot be established. That is this case: the notification fact is carried by no artifact. The case is escalated and it is terminal - no refund and no payment issues now, and the 0.86 SGD already adjusted, being the excess distance fare (deviation 1.20 km x fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd 0.72 = 0.86 SGD, POL-RD-24, no surge), is held pending review rather than collected from the driver or refunded to the rider. (5) Confidence and the rider's contrary argument. Confidence is 0.50, below the 0.80 that POL-RD-25 requires before the AI may rule on a route deviation. POL-GEN-22 puts a below-10.00 SGD dispute in the band the AI may decide, but POL-RD-25 adds the 0.80 bar for this category and it is not reachable on the decisive element, so the rider's request that the case simply be decided on the merits is rejected. Both parties' profiles are context only (POL-GEN-01) and decided nothing here. For the human reviewer: the question to answer is whether the driver notified the rider of the deviation before or at the point of deviation; it may help to check whether any trip call recording is held outside the evidence package and to weigh the rider's statement of 10 September 2026 against the driver's account."
  },
